{"step_index":2471,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T04:33:08Z","thinking":"**Crafting the C Runner**\n\nI'm now diving into the implementation of `sovra_bench_runner.c`. My focus is on creating a purely native C runner that can execute the six binaries, process their JSON outputs, and then format and print the empirical data as a table. The aim is to also generate `docs/audits/MULTILANG_18432D_SIDE_BY_SIDE_BENCHMARK.md` accurately.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// Pure Native C Orchestrator for SOVRA 5-Language Bare-Metal Benchmark Matrix\\n// Substrate: Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (Zero Python dependencies)\\n\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <unistd.h>\\n\\n#define MAX_OUT 8192\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    char name[128];\\n    char cmd[512];\\n    char cwd[512];\\n} Target;\\n\\nstatic void execute_and_capture(const char *cmd, const char *cwd, char *out_buf, size_t buf_size) {\\n    char full_cmd[1024];\\n    snprintf(full_cmd, sizeof(full_cmd), \\\"cd \\\\\\\"%s\\\\\\\" && %s 2>&1\\\", cwd, cmd);\\n    \\n    FILE *fp = popen(full_cmd, \\\"r\\\");\\n    if (!fp) {\\n        snprintf(out_buf, buf_size, \\\"❌ Failed to launch: %s\\\", full_cmd);\\n        return;\\n    }\\n\\n    size_t offset = 0;\\n    while (fgets(out_buf + offset, (int)(buf_size - offset), fp) != NULL) {\\n        offset = strlen(out_buf);\\n        if (offset >= buf_size - 1) break;\\n    }\\n    pclose(fp);\\n}\\n\\nint main(void) {\\n    printf(\\\"================================================================================\\\\n\\\");\\n    printf(\\\"  XORAS 5-LANGUAGE SIDE-BY-SIDE BARE-METAL NATIVE C BENCHMARK RUNNER\\\\n\\\");\\n    printf(\\\"  Substrate: Apple Silicon M4 (10 Cores) | 100,000 x 18,432-D Vectors (7.37 GB)\\\\n\\\");\\n    printf(\\\"================================================================================\\\\n\\\\n\\\");\\n\\n    const char *base_dir = \\\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/multilang_benchmark\\\";\\n    const char *rust_dir = \\\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/hexological_engine\\\";\\n    const char *report_path = \\\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/docs/audits/MULTILANG_18432D_SIDE_BY_SIDE_BENCHMARK.md\\\";\\n\\n    // 1. Build all 6 binaries\\n    printf(\\\"  [BUILD] Compiling C++20 kernel...\\\\n\\\");\\n    system(\\\"clang++ -O3 -std=c++20 -march=armv8.5-a /Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/multilang_benchmark/cpp/bench_18432d.cpp -o /Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/multilang\n<truncated 3874 bytes>","Description":"\"Pure native C benchmark runner without Python.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/workspaces/multilang_benchmark/sovra_bench_runner.c\"","toolAction":"\"Creating pure C benchmark orchestrator\"","toolSummary":"\"Write native C benchmark runner\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
